class:: SyncRingOsc
summary:: Carrier with two phase-synchronized ring modulators
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

SyncRingOsc derives two modulator phases from one signed carrier phase.
Integer ratios stay locked; fractional ratios reset to a deterministic phase
relationship on every carrier cycle. Two sequential amount controls crossfade
from the preceding signal to its ring product.

Sine, triangle, saw, and pulse shapes are available. Polynomial bandlimiting
handles nonsinusoidal edges, optional oversampling reduces modulation-product
aliasing, and fractional-ratio resets use a short correction ramp.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/SyncSaw::. Both establish a
repeatable phase relation, but SyncRingOsc derives two modulators from one
carrier, supports multiple shapes, and exposes the carrier, both modulators,
and final ring-modulated result.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Signed carrier frequency in hertz.

argument:: ratio1
First modulator ratio relative to the carrier, clamped to code::-64..64::.

argument:: ratio2
Second modulator ratio relative to the carrier, clamped to code::-64..64::.

argument:: amount1
Crossfade from carrier to carrier times modulator 1, clamped to code::0..1::.

argument:: amount2
Crossfade from the first result to that result times modulator 2, clamped to
code::0..1::.

argument:: phase1
First modulator phase offset in radians.

argument:: phase2
Second modulator phase offset in radians.

argument:: carrierWave
Initialization-rate carrier shape: code::0:: sine, code::1:: triangle,
code::2:: saw, or code::3:: pulse.

argument:: modWave1
Initialization-rate first-modulator shape using the same indices.

argument:: modWave2
Initialization-rate second-modulator shape using the same indices.

argument:: oversample
Initialization-rate value code::1::, code::2::, or code::4::.

argument:: mul
Multiplier applied to all four outputs.

argument:: add
Offset added to all four outputs after multiplication.

returns::
Four signals in this order: carrier, modulator 1, modulator 2, and sequential
ring-modulation result.

method:: kr

SyncRingOsc is audio-rate only. This method throws an error.

subsection:: Discussion

At code::amount1 = 0::, the first stage is exactly the carrier. At
code::amount2 = 0::, the second stage leaves the first unchanged. Amount one
selects the complete ring product. Feedback is not used, so all four outputs
remain phase coherent.

examples::

code::
(
{ SyncRingOsc.ar(90, 2, 3, 0.8)[3] * 0.075 }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
    var signal = SyncRingOsc.ar(
        55,
        LFNoise1.kr(0.2).range(1, 5),
        LFNoise1.kr(0.13).range(2, 9),
        amount1: 0.8, amount2: 0.6,
        modWave1: 1, modWave2: 2,
        oversample: 4
    );
    Splay.ar([signal[0], signal[3]]) * 0.045;
}.play;
)
::

